      "body": "Benchmarked on a single NVIDIA DGX Spark (GB10) for the Qwen3-Coder-Next-FP8 MoE shape (E=512, N=512, fp8_w8a8, block_shape=[128,128]). No existing config was found for this device, so vLLM fell back to the default config with a 'performance might be sub-optimal' warning on every boot.\r\n\r\n## Purpose \r\nNo tuned fused_moe config exists for NVIDIA GB10 (DGX Spark). vLLM falls back to a default config and logs a \"performance might be sub-optimal\" warning on every boot when serving Qwen3-Coder-Next-FP8 on this hardware.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\nRan vLLM's fused_moe kernel tuning benchmark on a single DGX Spark (GB10)  for the shape used by Qwen3-Coder-Next-FP8 (E=512, N=512, fp8_w8a8, block_shape=[128,128]). \r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\nWith the config in place, vLLM picks up the tuned kernel parameters automatically and the \"Using default MoE config\" warning no longer appears on startup. I think there's a mild speed boost from this but I didn't capture A/B test results.  \r\n",
